# Inertia Investment Management System - Coding Context

## Deploy target (mandatory)

| Workspace | Server |
|-----------|--------|
| **`Inertia2026-lean` (this tree)** | **KVM4** `187.127.188.97` — `./scripts/deployment/ship_kvm.sh` (preferred); Lean `129.121.133.25` — `./scripts/deployment/ship_lean.sh` (sunset) |
| **`app 2`** | BigRock `https://66.116.199.231/` / `inertiainvest.in` — deployment agent `full-prod` there only |

- **Never** deploy this tree to BigRock / `66.116.199.231` / `deploy_agent.py full-prod`.
- Refuse any request that would ship `Inertia2026-lean` code to BigRock.

## Architecture Overview

- **Stack**: Flask + SQLAlchemy, MySQL, Bootstrap frontend
- **Entry point**: `main.py` → `create_app()`, Gunicorn in production
- **Blueprints**: Registered in `main.py`; routes in `routes/`, APIs in `api/v1/`, `api/v2/`

## Directory Structure

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `routes/` | Flask route handlers (UI, forms, redirects) |
| `api/v1/`, `api/v2/` | REST API blueprints |
| `services/` | Business logic; use instead of routes for complex logic |
| `agents/` | Data-integrity & workflow agents (BaseAgent subclasses) |
| `models.py`, `models/` | SQLAlchemy models |
| `migrations/` | DB migrations (run manually) |
| `airflow/dags/` | Airflow DAGs for scheduled jobs |
| `templates/` | Jinja2 templates |
| `docs/` | Project documentation |
| `_deprecated/` | Legacy code; avoid adding dependencies on it |

## Conventions

### Business Logic
- Put business logic in **services**, not in route handlers
- Services are in `services/` (e.g. `task_assignment_service.py`, `price_service.py`)
- Routes should call services and handle HTTP/redirects only

### Agents (agents/)
- All agents subclass `BaseAgent` and implement `run_checks(client_id, **kwargs)` as a generator
- Agents yield `DataIntegrityIssue` objects; do NOT create alerts directly
- Register new agents in `agents/__init__.py`
- Agent runs are logged via `AgentRun`; use `start_run()`, `complete_run()`

### Task Assignment
- `TaskAssignmentRule`: rule_type in (`workflow_stage`, `issue_category`, `review_status`), match_value varies
- Workflow stages: FUNDS, RECOS, NOTIFY, EXEC, UPDATE, COMPLETED
- Review statuses: initiated, sent, meeting, closed
- Use `apply_review_assignment(workflow)` when creating/updating ReviewWorkflow
- Use `create_ops_task_from_issue()` / `create_ops_task_from_review_workflow()` to create OpsTasks for /tasks/
- Admin UI: `/admin/task-assignment-rules`

### Database
- Prefer `db.session` for writes; commit in route/service, not in models
- Migrations are Python scripts in `migrations/`; run with `python migrations/<file>.py`
- Models: `models.py` (large) + `models/` package

### Templates
- Extend `base.html` or `base_clean.html`
- CSRF: `{{ csrf_token() }}` in forms
- Flash messages: `get_flashed_messages(with_categories=true)`

### API
- Versioned: `/api/v1/`, `/api/v2/`
- Use `@login_required`, `require_advisor_or_manager` etc. for auth
- Return `jsonify({...})` for JSON APIs

## Key Domain Concepts

- **Client**: Portfolio owner; has advisor_id, planning_synopsis, review schedules
- **Workflow**: Monthly investment workflow; stages RECOS→FUNDS→NOTIFY→UPDATE→EXEC→COMPLETED
- **ReviewWorkflow**: Client review (initiated/sent/meeting/closed); has assigned_to
- **OpsTask**: Task in /tasks/; links to DataIntegrityIssue or ReviewWorkflow
- **DataIntegrityIssue**: Agent-created issue; has assigned_to, check_category, severity

## Avoid

- Adding logic to `routes/main.py` without extracting to services (file is very large)
- Using `ai_models` from `_deprecated/` without verifying it resolves; AI features may be disabled
- Direct DB queries in routes; prefer services
- Hardcoding user IDs; use TaskAssignmentRule for assignments

## Quick Reference

- Run migrations: `python migrations/<script>.py`
- Seed task rules: `python migrations/seed_task_assignment_rules.py`
- Backfill task assignment: Admin → Task Assignment Rules → Run Backfill
- Relevant docs: `docs/AGENTS_PROD_CHECK.md`, `docs/COMPREHENSIVE_DOCUMENTATION.md`
